==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|la|suppressus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|supprimō||press down or under}}, from {{m|la|sub||under}} + {{m|la|premō||press}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/səˈpɹɛs/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-suppress.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛs|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sup|press}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[put an end to]], especially with force, to [[crush]], [[do away with]]; to [[prohibit]], [[subdue]].
#: {{ux|en|Political dissent was brutally '''suppressed'''.}}
# To [[restrain]] or [[repress]], such as [[laughter]] or an [[expression]].
#: {{ux|en|I struggled to '''suppress''' my smile.}}
# {{lb|en|psychiatry}} To [[exclude]] undesirable thoughts from one's mind.
#: {{ux|en|He unconsciously '''suppressed''' his memories of abuse.}}
# To [[prevent]] publication.
#: {{ux|en|The government '''suppressed''' the findings of their research about the true state of the economy.}}
# To stop a [[flow]] or [[stream]].
#: {{ux|en|The rescue team managed to '''suppress''' the flow of oil by blasting the drilling hole.}}
#: {{ux|en|Hot blackcurrant juice mixed with honey may '''suppress''' cough.}}
# {{lb|en|US|legal}} To [[forbid]] the use of [[evidence]] at [[trial]] because it is [[improper]] or was improperly obtained.
# {{lb|en|electronics}} To [[reduce]] unwanted frequencies in a signal.
# {{lb|en|military}} To [[stop]] or [[prevent]] the enemy from executing unwanted activities like firing, regrouping, observation or others.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[hold]] in place, to keep [[low]].

